<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.6.7: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01356</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.6.7: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>ded6ccd3-bcb1-4fb5-b86e-67eef4d85d3d</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<para>Use the following passage to answer questions 1–3.</para>
<para>In a newly formed swamp, it is estimated that there are 500 mosquitoes. The population is estimated to double each
  day.</para>
<!--Do not edit this div tag.  It must surround the interaction block-->
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="3cf6c97f-83d5-4dec-85d7-596c9511d463" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--q1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="43fa5526-480c-4a1a-b106-126d453a95ff" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(m=500\cdot 2^d\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(m=d\\cdot 500^2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(m=2\\cdot 500^d\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(m=500\\cdot 2^d\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(m=500\\cdot d^2\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Let \(m\) represent the total population of mosquitoes and \(d\) represent the number of days that have
          passed since the first estimate. What is the equation that represents the growth of the mosquito population?
        </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.2.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="33b363a9-61f9-4568-9026-babbd59ea1e4" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="This represents 2 days before the first estimate was taken." data-solution-options="[&quot;This represents 2 days before the first estimate was taken.&quot;, &quot;This represents the day before the first estimate was taken.&quot;, &quot;This represents the day the first estimate was taken.&quot;, &quot;This represents 2 days after the first estimate was taken.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>What does \(d=-2\) represent in this context?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q3-->
  <exercise data-content-id="a3bf1633-9c98-468d-96b9-797888d0cabe" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="250" data-solution-options="[&quot;500&quot;, &quot;250&quot;, &quot;1,000&quot;, &quot;125&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the estimated number of mosquitoes that were in the new swamp 1 day before the estimate was taken?
        </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.2.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q4-->
  <!--Multiple Choice Starts here-->
  <exercise data-content-id="ad3dba8a-cb99-4c43-896e-7877ea939f47" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(v=40,000\cdot\left(\frac12\right)^y\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y=40,000\\cdot\\left(\\frac12\\right)^v\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(v=40,000\\cdot\\left(\\frac12\\right)^y\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(v=20,000\\cdot\\left(\\frac14\\right)^y\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(v=\\frac12\\cdot\\left(40,000\\right)^y\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Use the following passage to answer questions 4–6.</para>
      <para>A desert pond is slowly drying up. The average volume of the pond is shown in the table. The first year it was
        measured, the average volume was determined to be 40,000 liters. Double click on mathematical
        expression/equation to enlarge.</para>
      <table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
        <thead>
          <row>
            <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">\(y\), years</entry>
            <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">\(v\), volume (liters)</entry>
          </row>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry>
              –4
            </entry>
            <entry> </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              –2
            </entry>
            <entry> </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              0
            </entry>
            <entry>
              40,000
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              1
            </entry>
            <entry>
              20,000
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              3
            </entry>
            <entry>
              5,000
            </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <para> Which equation represents the pond’s water loss?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para dir="ltr" id="docs-internal-guid-075012a3-7fff-c3c9-5f23-c6c4e020927f">Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="1aa16586-e2a9-4f03-81ba-c6cefedf6bc6" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="the time 2 years before the first time the volume was measured" data-solution-options="[&quot;the time it took for the pond to shrink by a factor of 2&quot;, &quot;the first time the volume was measured&quot;, &quot;the time 2 years after the first time the volume was measured&quot;, &quot;the time 2 years before the first time the volume was measured&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>What does \(y=-2\) represent in this context?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.3.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="0523a23f-0076-4431-b856-a144c4d029a5" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="640,000 liters" data-solution-options="[&quot;320,000 liters&quot;, &quot;160,000 liters&quot;, &quot;80,000 liters&quot;, &quot;640,000 liters&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> What was the average volume of the pond 4 years before the first time the volume was measured?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.3.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q7-->
  <exercise data-content-id="f289d931-83cb-4e3b-adad-e0ecce980124" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(6.35\times 10^6\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(6.35\\times 10^4\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(6.35\\times 10^5\\) &quot;, &quot;\\(6.35\\times 10^6\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(6.35\\times 10^7\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which of the following is equivalent to 6,350,000 in scientific notation?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.4.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q8-->
  <exercise data-content-id="9de6da24-490a-47d4-a381-5749a1a2ba48" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(3.2\times 10^{-4}\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(3.2\\times 10^{-3}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(3.2\\times 10^{-4}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(3.2\\times 10^{-5}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(3.2\\times 10^{-6}\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which of the following is equivalent to 0.00032 in scientific notation?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.4.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q9-->
  <exercise data-content-id="643511df-673b-4103-a6a5-761446059723" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="7,240" data-solution-options="[&quot;7,240&quot;, &quot;724&quot;, &quot;72,400&quot;, &quot;724,000&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which of the following is equivalent to \(7.24\times 10^3\) in decimal form?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q10-->
  <exercise data-content-id="31765884-975f-46fe-b3d1-76599c96e5d4" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="0.0000547" data-solution-options="[&quot;0.00547&quot;, &quot;0.0000547&quot;, &quot;0.00000547&quot;, &quot;0.000547&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which of the following is equivalent to \(5.47\times 10^{-5}\) in decimal form?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--q11-->
  <exercise data-content-id="a543be8b-3931-41cd-87a0-e0cb9643cf50" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="Value S, Value R, Value U, Value T" data-solution-options="[&quot;Value S, Value R, Value T, Value U&quot;, &quot;Value R, Value S, Value T, Value U&quot;, &quot;Value S, Value R, Value U, Value T&quot;, &quot;Value R, Value S, Value U, Value T&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> Which of the following correctly orders these values from greatest to least?
          <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
            <thead/>
            <tbody>
              <row>
                <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Value R</entry>
                <entry>
                  0.00161
                </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Value S</entry>
                <entry>
                  \(6.35\times 10^{-3}\)
                </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Value T</entry>
                <entry>
                  0.000541
                </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Value U</entry>
                <entry>
                  \(7.23\times 10^{-4}\)
                </entry>
              </row>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 5.6.5.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution>
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
  </div>
</div></section>
